    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><ref refid="classthemis_1_1security_1_1_i_t_s_a_client" kindref="compound">ITSAClient</ref> — abstract RFC 3161 Timestamp Authority client.</para>
<para>All production code and tests should depend on this interface, not on the concrete <ref refid="classthemis_1_1security_1_1_t_s_a_client_wrapper" kindref="compound">TSAClientWrapper</ref> or <ref refid="classthemis_1_1security_1_1_timestamp_authority" kindref="compound">TimestampAuthority</ref> classes.</para>
<para>Thread safety: implementations are not required to be thread-safe. Callers must ensure serialised access or use one instance per thread. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
